A system tray at the right end of the bar: programs dock their icons in it
by the freedesktop.org tray protocol and XEmbed, and the status moves left
to make room. Upstream's systray patch, with these changes:

- An icon that asks to be hidden, by clearing XEMBED_MAPPED, is hidden and
  takes no room. Upstream ignored flags of 0, mapped every icon on each
  update, and mapped an icon again whenever it unmapped itself.
- A map request from an icon is not taken for a window to manage.
- On exit, and on a restart before dwm execs itself, the icons go back to
  the root window, unmapped and out of the save-set, as XEmbed ends an
  embedding. Upstream destroyed them with the tray on exit, and a restart,
  which execs before cleanup(), left X to map them on the root window,
  where the next dwm managed them as windows. Their programs dock them in
  the next tray.
- _XEMBED_INFO's flags are read when the property has its two items, by
  the item count 6.8's getatomprop() keeps.
- Icons are systrayiconsize high (config.h), centred in the bar.

Only XEmbed icons dock. A program that offers its icon only as a
StatusNotifierItem over D-Bus needs a bridge to show here, such as
snixembed.

